    description: "From WI-borib (docs/audits/0026). Verdict SINGLE-SOURCE.\n\ncmd_dead_code_maybe rebuilds each node into a Symbol by hand for detect_entrypoints (cli.py ~9408-9430), keeping id/name/kind/language/discovery_language/protocol_origin/path/span/meta and dropping supply_chain (tier) and modifiers. The edges on the same path already go through Edge.from_dict for exactly this reason (WI-higap, INV-nudoj). So the one shared helper, detect_entrypoints, gets different inputs in dead-code than in survey/slice/sketch: agent A's map (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/borib_consumer_agreement_10302026/A_runs/synth.json) with one export set to tier 3 -- slice, sketch and the persisted entrypoints drop it, dead-code keeps it as a seed at rank 0.84.\n\nNOT measured on a real repo (dead-code does not print its seeds; agent A's appendix has an in-process diff). ACCEPTANCE: the rebuild goes through the one Symbol deserializer; a test that detect_entrypoints over dead-code's Symbols equals it over the survey's on a map with a tier-3 export."  # 96a6
